      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this should also explain why it\u0027s not possible to update the mark in to make it less specific, and what happens if userspace tries to do that (ENOENT?).\n\nI think the answer is that this operation is fundamentally ambiguous because the mark attribute coming from userspace is used both to find the existing SA and as the new value to set in the SA. That suggests that it\u0027s actually possible to update the mark in the general case, but it would require adding a new netlink attribute.\n\nThat makes this approach feel a little hacky, but seems it would be better to have the hackiness be explicit and addressed in the commit message as a known issue that was considered than left for reviewers to notice.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 10,
        "startChar": 30,
        "endLine": 11,
        "endChar": 20
      },
      "revId": "941e82e9f85ba13b2d13312fa7766a704e4f6a1c",
